---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Colour Transfer & Automated Colour Grading - François Pitié" currentSection="research">
  <div class="post">
    <header class="post-header mb-8">
      <div class="mb-2">
        <a href="/research" class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)]">&larr; back to research</a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="post-title">Colour Transfer & Automated Colour Grading</h1>
      <p class="desc text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1.5 pb-3 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)]">
        Mathematical formulations for probability density transfer and continuous Monge-Kantorovich optimal transport.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-10">
      <!-- Hero Visual -->
      <div class="rounded overflow-hidden border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)] shadow-xs">
        <img 
          src="/images/colourtransfer.jpg" 
          alt="Colour Transfer: Original, Target Palette, and After Transfer" 
          class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
        />
        <div class="p-3 text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] border-t border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/70">
          <strong>Figure: </strong> Example of colour transfer — (left) original image, (centre) target colour palette image, (right) resulting image after continuous distribution transfer.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview -->
      <section class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-[var(--theme-fg)] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong>Colour Transfer</strong> is the process of matching colour characteristics and colorimetric moods between different photographic images or video sequences. The fundamental challenge is determining a bijective transformation in 3D colour space that aligns the joint probability density function (PDF) of a source image with that of a reference grade without introducing contouring or gamut artefacts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our research introduced an exact, iterative solution to multi-dimensional probability density function transfer based on 1D Radon projections, alongside closed-form linear Monge-Kantorovich formulations. These mathematical frameworks became the technological foundation for commercial grading tools, notably <em>MatchGrade</em> in The Foundry's <strong>Furnace</strong> suite for Nuke.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Open Source Code & Resources -->
      <section class="p-4 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/40">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--theme-heading)] mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <i class="fa-brands fa-github text-base"></i>
          Reference Implementation & Code
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--theme-muted)] mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          Reference MATLAB code implementing the iterative N-dimensional PDF transfer algorithm, the linear Monge-Kantorovich mapping, and post-filtering regraining routines.
        </p>
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/frcs/colour-transfer" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer" 
          class="pub-btn"
        >
          frcs/colour-transfer on GitHub &rarr;
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Publications -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-light tracking-tight text-[var(--theme-heading)] pb-2 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)] mb-4">
          Key Publications
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              Automated colour grading using colour distribution transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié, A. Kokaram, and R. Dahyot
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              Computer Vision and Image Understanding (CVIU), 107(1-2):123–137, 2007.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              The linear Monge-Kantorovitch linear colour mapping for example-based colour transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié and A. Kokaram
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              4th European Conference on Visual Media Production (CVMP), London, 2007.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              N-Dimensional Probability Density Function Transfer and its Application to Colour Transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié, A. Kokaram, and R. Dahyot
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              Tenth IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), Beijing, 2005.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
